        <body>
            <div xml:id="d953">

                <pb facs="0995" n="875" xml:id="pg875"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00 Johnson Electoral Mission/196:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Hanna</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-05-12T15:00:00-05:45">May 12, 1931—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 6:40 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>74. Your 115, May 11, 6 p.m. I have been awaiting a favorable opportunity to take
                    up with President Moncada the designation of Major Price. It is very
                    embarrassing to propose the contemplated arrangement because of the salary which
                    this Government will be expected to pay Major Price. The amount is small by our
                    standards but this Government will consider it a real drain on its revenues at
                    this time. Many of its high officials are receiving practically no salary at
                    present. I hope the Department of State or the Navy Department can give Major
                    Price an appropriate allowance for this tour of duty only. This would be
                    appreciated by this Government and would help me materially in my
                    representations.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hanna</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
